      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Isolated coronary ostial narrowing is rare and most often attributed to atherosclerotic disease of the aorta. A man with isolated, bilateral stenoses of the coronary ostia is presented, who also had severe peripheral vascular disease. A review of previous reports concerning coronary ostial disease is presented."},
